    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (79.78) and **Junior Caminero** (76.37). **Yordan Alvarez** remains our most potent offensive threat; despite a slightly neutral park factor, his elite .460 xwOBA and favorable matchup against Ginn make him a mandatory start. **Junior Caminero** benefits significantly from a +16% park adjustment today, pushing his output into the elite tier despite a moderate matchup against the southpaw Rogers. Meanwhile, the ZEBRA priority on stolen bases is reflected in the strong scores for **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (69.51) and **Trea Turner** (66.09); **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is maximized by an leadoff spot and a dynamic platoon advantage, while **Trea Turner** remains a high-floor play despite a competent Dobbins on the hill.\n\nThe lineup construction reflects a firm commitment to our efficiency floor, evidenced by the exclusion of **Jacob Gonzalez** (37.99) and **Gary Sanchez** (37.56). **Jacob Gonzalez** was the most difficult exclusion; his potential was capped by a difficult matchup against Yamamoto and a bottom-third order placement that plummeted his scoring projection below our 40-point threshold. We are also monitoring the volatility surrounding **Kazuma Okamoto** (42.03) and **Pedro Ramirez** (40.59); both are currently active but sit dangerously close to the bench floor due to difficult matchups against Schlittler and Hancock, respectively. **Dillon Dingler** (57.10) and **Caleb Durbin** (56.33) round out the mid-tier, providing stable production, though both require careful monitoring of the game flow to ensure they reach their projected plate appearances. With no significant weather flags, the primary risk remains the high-caliber SP_xERA profiles of Schlittler and Yamamoto, which could suppress offensive output if our hitters fail to capitalize on the limited high-leverage opportunities provided.",
